# testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime (ir/AOTEffectsNet.h, SecondLaneInEffectsNet): a second word of digests of each operand, for the heaps that the first word has no lane for.
# f6 = the arrow function in makeCounter
# RUN(NET): run-in-shell testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime mechanisms=all
# NET: 7
# NET-NEXT: 2
# NET-NEXT: 1
# NET-NEXT: 18
# NET-NEXT: went on
# The lie, testing=RowSaysLess: one row is taken not to write one heap.
# RUN(BYTES): run-in-shell testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime,RowSaysLess:Builtin/%TypedArray%.prototype.fill/TypedArrayElements mechanisms=all
# BYTES: say that the call will not write TypedArrayElements, and of operand {{*}} these are others behind it: the bytes. This is a bug in Bun.
# BYTES-NOT: went on
# BYTES: crashed
# BYTES: with
# RUN(REGEXP): run-in-shell testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime,RowSaysLess:Builtin/RegExp.prototype.exec/RegExpState mechanisms=all
# REGEXP: say that the call will not write RegExpState, and of operand {{*}} these are others behind it: the state of the regular expression. This is a bug in Bun.
# REGEXP-NOT: went on
# REGEXP: crashed
# REGEXP: with
# RUN(PROTOTYPE): run-in-shell testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime,RowSaysLess:Builtin/Object.setPrototypeOf/PrototypeLinks mechanisms=all
# PROTOTYPE: say that the call will not write PrototypeLinks, and of operand {{*}} these are others behind it: the prototype. This is a bug in Bun.
# PROTOTYPE-NOT: went on
# PROTOTYPE: crashed
# PROTOTYPE: with
# What Link says of a callee: the variable that the closure holds in its environment.
# RUN(ENVIRONMENT): run-in-shell testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime,RowSaysLess:Callee/f6/EnvironmentFields mechanisms=all
# ENVIRONMENT: say that the call will not write EnvironmentFields, and of operand {{*}} these are others behind it: the variables of the environment. This is a bug in Bun.
